Summary of rStar2-Agent (from README + paper 2508.20722):
- Method: Agentic RL with Python tool-use in a secure Code Judge environment; multi-turn rollouts; prompt with <reason>/<answer> and function-call format for tools.
- Algorithm: GRPO-RoC (Group Relative Policy Optimization + Resample-on-Correct). Oversample rollouts, downsample negatives uniformly, filter positives by tool-error ratio and format violations to prefer higher quality successes. Answer-only rewards to avoid reward hacking. Clip-Higher (epsilon_high=0.28), no KL, no entropy bonus.
- Infra: VERL-based RL with SGLang/VLLM for inference; isolated high-throughput code execution service via Redis + async workers; dynamic load-balanced rollout scheduler.
- Recipe: Non-reasoning SFT (instruction following + tool format) then 3 RL stages with max response lengths 8K→12K→12K and difficulty filtering in stage 3. Batch ~512 prompts; oversample 32, select 16 via RoC; T turns 10/10/15; LR 1e-6 AdamW.
- Results: 14B model reaches 80.6% AIME24, 69.8% AIME25 in 510 RL steps; shorter responses vs baselines. Lessons: keep truncated rollouts as negative; avoid overly complex intermediate penalties.

Implications for Gemma-3-12B-IT + Unsloth:

Clarifying Questions for User Approval:
Answered by user:
- SFT-first now; later full-fledged tool-caller coder.
- Combine Unsloth with rStar infra acceptable; 32GB constraint acknowledged; can drop to 7B if needed.
- Start with GSM8K (math), later coding; split eval from train.
- Expose max_seq_len and all knobs via YAML.
- Prefer SFT + RL overall.
- Provide single script to start services; assume Docker & Compose.
- Best metric: lowest eval_loss.
- Eval split ratio configurable in YAML.
- JSONL inputs with keys configurable.
- QLoRA primary; allow RSLoRA switch if compatible.
- Single-GPU only.
